meta {
  name: 6 Remove time off
  type: http
  seq: 6
}
delete {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/calendar/blocks/{{providerEmail}}/{{calendarBlockIdentifier}}
}
docs {
  Removes one of the provider's own blocks. Fill `calendarBlockIdentifier` from a
  `3 List time off` response.

  **Removal matters as much as creating one:** a cancelled trip that still blocks the calendar costs the
  provider bookings they never meant to refuse.

  The owning email is in the delete's own **filter**, not checked beforehand, so it cannot be raced into
  removing somebody else's block.

  `204` on success, `404` when no such block exists for this provider. Deliberately **not** 204-regardless,
  unlike `DELETE /device-token`: whether a provider holds a given block of their own is not information
  withheld from them, and a silent success would hide a client sending the wrong identifier.

  Verify with `1 Availability`: those hours are bookable again.
}
